<div id="features" class="features">
  <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="capture-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="capture-title">Highlight in Safari. Keep the source.</h2>
      <p>Select text on a page and press <kbd>⌃⇧H</kbd>, or turn on auto-highlight and just read. Twine saves the passage with the page title and a link back, and highlights it again whenever you return.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>Highlight from the keyboard, or automatically as you read</li>
        <li>Highlights come back when you revisit a page, as long as its text is still there</li>
        <li>A link to a highlight opens the page scrolled to the passage</li>
        <li>Option-click a highlight to remove it, and undo from the page</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="media">
      {% shot "capture", "mac", "The training section of Wikipedia's large language model article in Safari, with the passage about model training costs highlighted in yellow.", "Safari on a public article with one or two saved Twine highlights. No transient messages or recording needed.", false, "macOS · Save a passage in Safari", 2200, 1584 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature feature-library" aria-labelledby="library-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="library-title">Find any passage again.</h2>
      <p>Browse by website and page, search the words you remember, and narrow by period. Copy a passage with its link, or share it as plain text or Markdown.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>Organized by website and page</li>
        <li>Search highlight text, page titles and websites</li>
        <li>Syncs to your iPhone through your private iCloud</li>
        <li>Shows up in Spotlight and opens from Shortcuts</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="media">
      {% shot "library-duo", "duo", "An open Duo with Twine's All Highlights library on the left and the selected Wikipedia training-cost passage, background explanation and actions on the right.", "The open Duo in landscape orientation, with the library and selected highlight details visible side by side.", false, "Duo · Your library and the details, side by side", 2812, 2034 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="ai-title">Let your AI tools read your highlights.</h2>
      <p>Turn on AI Access and Twine runs a read-only MCP server on your Mac. Compatible AI tools can search your highlights, read the passages and point you back to the pages.</p>
      <ul class="prompts" role="list" aria-label="Example requests">
        <li>Find my highlights about onboarding and group them by theme.</li>
        <li>Compare what my saved sources say about remote work, with links to each page.</li>
        <li>Use my highlights from the past week to outline a research brief, and list the excerpts you used.</li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>Off until you turn it on, and reachable only from your Mac</li>
        <li>Protected by an access token you can replace at any time</li>
        <li>Tools can search, read and export your highlights, but never change them</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">Example requests for a connected AI tool, not a built-in Twine chat. Responses depend on your tool and the highlights you've saved.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="media media-settings">
      {% shot "ai-access", "window", "Twine's AI settings on a Mac with AI Access enabled, a local server URL and controls to copy connection settings or regenerate the token; no token value is displayed.", "Twine Settings > AI > AI Access, with the local server enabled and connection controls visible. Keep access tokens concealed; no chat response needed.", false, "macOS · Connect the AI tools you choose", 1040, 1436 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="context-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="context-title">See how a passage fits.</h2>
      <p>Turn on AI context and Twine uses Apple Intelligence, on your device, to explain how a highlight fits into the text around it. The explanation is saved with the highlight and syncs with it.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>Written on your device, never by a server-based model</li>
        <li>Off by default, and you can refresh an explanation at any time</li>
        <li>Needs a device where Apple Intelligence is available and turned on</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="media">
      {% shot "context", "phone", "An iPhone showing the highlighted Wikipedia training-cost passage, a completed AI Context explanation, the Refresh control and the source.", "An iPhone highlight detail with a completed AI context explanation. Use a public passage with enough surrounding text; avoid loading or unavailable states.", false, "iPhone · Read a passage in context", 1206, 2622 %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="privacy-title">Your library stays yours.</h2>
    <div>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>No Twine account. There's nothing to sign up for.</li>
        <li>Highlights live on your devices and sync through your private iCloud. The developer never receives them.</li>
        <li>No analytics, ads or trackers, in the app or on this site.</li>
        <li>AI access is off until you turn it on, and it stays on your Mac. A tool you connect handles what it reads under its own privacy policy.</li>
      </ul>
